      "content": "The patchy spots likely result from inconsistent fabric tension or localized gaps in your press, causing intermittent pressure and heat distribution. Polyester garments bleed when overheated or exposed to inconsistent temperature, so 200°C might be too high for your specific setup. You should increase the pressure slightly to a constant 6 bar and ensure the fabric is under full tension before applying heat to eliminate air pockets.",
