      "content": "Yes, the issue could definitely stem from sublimation paper or ink compatibility with your specific polyester fibers. If the ink solubility is mismatched with the fiber type, it will degrade and fail to set even under uniform heat and pressure. Additionally, ensure the sublimation paper is rated precisely for your polyester grade, as using the wrong paper source can cause the dye to melt away entirely instead of bonding. I recommend testing a different batch of paper to rule out a manufacturing defect before adjusting your settings further.",
