      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You shouldn't observe ink \"vanishing\" mid-transfer; sublimation ink bonds chemically into the polyester fibers once the correct heat is reached after the initial heating begins. The patchy gaps you are seeing are likely caused by air pockets trapped within the fabric threads, which prevents the ink from making direct, full contact with the fiber at those specific points. Even if the ink solidifies before fully releasing into the fiber, the incomplete transfer will leave solid-looking areas where the ink has only partially reacted or remains on the surface, creating those faulty looks. To resolve this, ensure you are peeling the sublimation paper at the correct temperature (before the ink moves entirely) and verify there are no wrinkles in the fabric.",
